# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 2a (partner opens 1C). The PDF hand has 14 cards; one diamond removed.
title: Partner opens 1♣: show your spades
id: L02-04
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.6
student: S
board: 4
dealer: W
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A85    K65    QJT    KJ65
  E  Q93    JT98   A87    Q43
  S  JT764  AQ2    943    T7
  W  K2     743    K652   A982

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 1S*    = 6+ points, four or more spades
     key: 7 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton is 8, and five spades. Show them at the one level.
     not Pass: Did you count 8? With 6 or more, find a response.
     not 2C: With only two clubs, can you raise partner?
     not 1NT: You have a spade suit to show. Did you look at that option?
     not 2S: A jump to 2♠ isn't in our system. 1♠ shows spades and 6+ points.
     not *: With 6+ points and four or more spades, which response shows them?
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = A balanced minimum, 13-14
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: about 22 points
     key: Partner showed 13-14. With your 8, your side has about 22. Stop.
     not 2S: Partner chose no-trump. With so little extra, let her play 1NT.
     not 2NT: Did you add it up? 8 plus 13-14 is well short of 25.
     not 3NT: Did you add it up? 8 plus 13-14 is well short of 25.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your 1♠ showed four or more spades and 6+ points. Partner's 1NT said she
  has a balanced minimum and fewer than four spades. With your 8, your
  side has about 22: no game, so pass. North is declarer, because she bid
  no-trump first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E HJ  S H2  W H3  N HK
  2   N SA  E S3  S S4  W S2
      note: Declarer's plan: set up dummy's spades. Start with the ♠A.
  3   N S5  E S9  S ST  W SK
      note: Another spade, to drive out the king.
  4   W D2  N DT  E DA  S D3
  5   E D8  S D4  W DK  N DJ
  6   W D6  N DQ  E D7  S D9
  7   N S8  E SQ  S S6  W C9
      note: Another spade, to drive out the queen.
  8   E C3  S C7  W CA  N C5
  9   W D5  N H5  E H8  S CT
  10  W C8  N CK  E C4  S S7
      note: Declarer's ♣K wins.
  11  N H6  E H9  S HQ  W H4
      note: A heart over to dummy.
  12  S HA  W H7  N C6  E HT
      note: The ♥A.
  13  S SJ  W C2  N CJ  E CQ
      note: Dummy's last spade is a winner. 7 tricks: 1NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: set up dummy's long spades, keeping the ♥A and ♥Q to
  reach them.

  1NT made. Your side had 21 HCP, and the part score was the right place
  to stop.
